ed in free play.  \n\nGiven our hand has rockets and two 2s as high control, leading with a small pair (♥5 ♣5) is reasonable because it conserves our high cards, tests the Landlord\'s response, and might allow our teammate to take control if they have a better pair. It also starts to reduce our hand\'s fragmented nature.  \n\nReason: Leading with a low pair applies moderate pressure without overcommitting high cards, aligns with reducing our hand\'s weakness in pairs, and keeps rockets and 2s for later critical plays against potential bombs or high combinations from the Landlord.  \n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥5", "♣5"]}'}
